# Two batches mention detection 0, and the field map's FIRST candidate must win.
#
# This is the case `records.h` said could not happen -- "a batch only ever holds rows of ITS
# OWN class" -- and the resolved chain plan can now produce it: a crop slot with no
# `classes:` covers every row beside a per-class one. Both planes overwrote, so the LAST
# batch to mention a row set the field; both take the first now, and this pins it.
scenario first_candidate_wins
camera cam0
frame 7
source shard-0
size 1920 1080
fps 20.0
captured_unix_ns 1700000000000000000
emitted_unix_ns 1700000001000000000
finished complete

# A ship is 8 in this checkout's detector, and a person is 0.
label 0 person
label 8 ship

# index class_id score  x1  y1  x2  y2
det 0 8 0.875 100 200 300 400
det 1 0 0.5 10 20 30 40

# The per-class batch, covering the ship row only.
batch embed_ship_out 2
row 0 0.25 0.5

# The every-row batch, covering both. Declared SECOND in the field map below, so it must not
# overwrite row 0 -- and it must still fill row 1, which nothing else covers.
batch embed_any_out 2
row 0 0.75 0.875
row 1 2.0 3.0

field embedding embed_ship_out embed_any_out
